{
  "_": [
    "THE CURATED GIBS LAYER SET — the hand-kept half of assets/catalog.json.",
    "",
    "Every id here was checked to exist in NASA's own Worldview configuration",
    "(nasa-gibs/worldview, config/default/common/config/wv.json/layers/**). The",
    "machine-readable half — imagery resolution (which becomes the WMTS tile",
    "matrix set), temporal resolution, and the layer description — is parsed out",
    "of that same checkout by make-catalog.mjs, so this file only carries what a",
    "human has to decide: which layers are worth a place, what to call them, when",
    "the record starts, and where they sit in the browser.",
    "",
    "fmt is derived (base imagery = jpg, anything drawn over it = png) and can be",
    "overridden per layer. 'set' and 'period' can be overridden the same way when",
    "the upstream description does not state a resolution.",
    "",
    "start dates are the beginning of the GIBS record where it is known, and the",
    "instrument's own start otherwise. A start that is too late only hides old",
    "days; the map itself never lies about a day with no data — it says so."
  ],

